  "content": "Config has three resolution layers, applied in order (last wins): (1) global `config.toml` in repo root, (2) repo-committed `.yullu/config.toml` for team-shared knobs like sync_dir and dreaming, (3) user-private `~/.config/yullu/projects/\u003csanitized_project_id\u003e.toml` for personal stuff like API keys. Layer 2 strips api_key fields on load (committed files must not carry secrets) — warnings surface via the GET /api/projects/{id}/overrides response. Embedding provider/model deliberately CANNOT be overridden per project (the SQLite store locks embed_id + embed_dim at first write — changing per project would corrupt the vector index). Phase 2c TODO: per-project API keys are stored but the running embedder/reasoner still uses global keys; ~12 call sites need threading via Server.embedderForProject / reasonerForProject lookups.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"config\", \"architecture\", \"todo\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
